2 TITL About Catherine Penistone
1 _OID 02e1ec13-94cc-44dd-8acb-d98fc1655a14
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;div style="margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border-bottom: 1px dashed #eeeeee; color: #333333; font-family: arial, 'helvetica neue', helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12px;"&gt;</line><line>&lt;strong&gt;About Catherine Pe
2 CONC nistone&lt;/strong&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;div style="margin: 0px; padding: 5px 0px 0px; overflow-wrap: break-word; word-break: break-word; color: #333333; font-family: arial, 'helvetica neue', helvetica, sans-serif; font-size
2 CONC : 12px;"&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin: 10px 0px 15px; padding: 0px; line-height: 17px;"&gt;Catherine Penistone&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;ul style="margin: 0px 0px 15px; padding: 0px; list-style: none;"&gt;</line><line>&lt;li style="margin: 0
2 CONC px 0px 0px 30px; padding: 2px 0px; list-style-type: disc; color: #444444;"&gt;Birth: 1440 - of Coverto Pramote, Pi&amp;eacute;mont, Italy &amp;nbsp; [2]&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li style="margin: 0px 0px 0px 30px; padding: 2px 0px; list
2 CONC -style-type: disc; color: #444444;"&gt;Parents: Gregory Penistone, Born 1415 in Courtesello, Italy (Penison or Peniston of Coursello, Provence)&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li style="margin: 0px 0px 0px 30px; padding: 2px 0px; list-style-type: disc
2 CONC ; color: #444444;"&gt;Married: Bef 22 Dec 1456&amp;nbsp; Courtecello, Italy &amp;nbsp; [2]&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li style="margin: 0px 0px 0px 30px; padding: 2px 0px; list-style-type: disc; color: #444444;"&gt;Spouse: William Vaux (1
2 CONC 435-1471)&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li style="margin: 0px 0px 0px 30px; padding: 2px 0px; list-style-type: disc; color: #444444;"&gt;AKA: Katherine; Penyston, Pennison, Peniston&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;/ul&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin: 1
2 CONC 0px 0px 15px; padding: 0px; line-height: 17px;"&gt;Children include&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;ol style="margin: 0px 0px 15px; padding: 0px; list-style: none;"&gt;</line><line>&lt;li style="margin: 0px 0px 0px 30px; padding: 2px 0px; list-style-type
2 CONC : decimal; color: #444444;"&gt;Sir Nicholas Vaux b abt 1460 in Harrowden, Northamptonshire, England. Married 1) Elizabeth FitzHugh 2) Anne Green&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li style="margin: 0px 0px 0px 30px; padding: 2px 0px; list-style-type: decim
2 CONC al; color: #444444;"&gt;Joan (Jane) b abt 1462 Married 1) Sir Richard Guildford 2) Anthony Poyntz&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;/ol&gt;</line><line>brief biography</line><line>&lt;ul style="margin: 0px 0px 15px; padding: 0px; list-style: none;"&gt;</l
2 CONC ine><line>&lt;li style="margin: 0px 0px 0px 30px; padding: 2px 0px; list-style-type: disc; color: #444444;"&gt;from&amp;nbsp;VAUX, Sir Nicholas (c.1460-1523), of Great Harrowden, Northants.&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;/ul&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style
2 CONC ="margin: 10px 0px 15px; padding: 0px; line-height: 17px;"&gt;Nicholas Vaux&amp;rsquo;s mother&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Catherine,&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;an attendant on Queen Margaret of Anjou, remained constant to her mistress when others forsoo
2 CONC k the Lancastrian cause. Her husband,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Sir William Vaux of Great Harrowden&lt;/strong&gt;, whom she had married not long before she obtained her letters of denization, was slain at the battle of Tewkesbury after which he was a
2 CONC ttainted and his property forfeited, but not even his death shook&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Catherine Vaux&amp;rsquo;s&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;loyalty: she stayed by the Queen during her imprisonment in the Tower and on Margaret&amp;rsquo;s release i
2 CONC n 1476 went with her into exile (as she had done earlier in the 1460s), living with her until her death six years later.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin: 10px 0px 15px; padding: 0px; line-height: 17px;"&gt;Catherine&amp;rsquo;s&amp;nbsp;&
2 CONC lt;strong&gt;two&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;children did not share either her confinement or her travels abroad; instead, Nicholas Vaux was brought up in the household of Margaret, Countess of Richmond, without charge even though Edward IV restored tw
2 CONC o manors to the family for the maintenance of him and his sister.4&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin: 10px 0px 15px; padding: 0px; line-height: 17px;"&gt;Catherine&amp;rsquo;s devotion was rewarded after the triumph of Henry VII at Bosworth
2 CONC , where Nicholas Vaux, as a prot&amp;eacute;g&amp;eacute; of Margaret Beaufort, probably fought under her husband Lord Stanley; the petition for the reversal of the attainder on Vaux&amp;rsquo;s father and the forfeiture of his property was accepte
2 CONC d by the King in the Parliament of 1485, and not long after Vaux was named to the commission of the peace for his home county.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin: 10px 0px 15px; padding: 0px; line-height: 17px;"&gt;He fought for the King a
2 CONC t Stoke and Blackheath, being knighted on the field for his service in both battles. Not only was he active and diligent in local government but he was also frequently at court attending all the great state occasions at home and abroad until his de
2 CONC ath; in 1511 he entertained Henry VIII at Harrowden. It was as a soldier and diplomat, however, that he made his mark. Given the important command at Guisnes, he distinguished himself during the Tournai campaign in 1513 and then in the missions (h
2 CONC e had had some earlier experiences in negotiating, chiefly with Burgundy) to the French King about the English withdrawal and the several royal marriage treaties. Later, he was one of the devisers of the Field of Cloth of Gold.&lt;/p&gt;</line><lin
2 CONC e>&lt;p style="margin: 10px 0px 15px; padding: 0px; line-height: 17px;"&gt;Her daughter Joan had also benefited from the change of dynasty: she entered the royal household, became governess to Henry VII&amp;rsquo;s daughters and married successivel
2 CONC y Sir Richard Guildford and the father of Sir Nicholas Poyntz.5&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin: 10px 0px 15px; padding: 0px; line-height: 17px;"&gt;Notes&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;ul style="margin: 0px 0px 15px; padding: 0px; list-style
2 CONC : none;"&gt;</line><line>&lt;li style="margin: 0px 0px 0px 30px; padding: 2px 0px; list-style-type: disc; color: #444444;"&gt;alternate spelling of birth place: Courtesello, Piedmont, Italy&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;/ul&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style
2 CONC ="margin: 10px 0px 15px; padding: 0px; line-height: 17px;"&gt;Sources&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;ol style="margin: 0px 0px 15px; padding: 0px; list-style: none;"&gt;</line><line>&lt;li style="margin: 0px 0px 0px 30px; padding: 2px 0px; list-style-ty
2 CONC pe: decimal; color: #444444;"&gt;[S20] Magna Carta Ancestry: A study in Colonial and Medieval Families, Richardson, Douglas, (Kimball G. Everingham, editor. 2nd edition, 2011), vol. 3 p. 289.&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li style="margin: 0px 0px 0p
2 CONC x 30px; padding: 2px 0px; list-style-type: decimal; color: #444444;"&gt;[S211] #1001 The Victoria History of the Counties of England Hertfordshire, Page, William, (4 volumes. London 1971.), FHL book Q 942 H2vher., vol. 1 p. 395.&lt;/li&gt;</line><l
2 CONC ine>&lt;li style="margin: 0px 0px 0px 30px; padding: 2px 0px; list-style-type: decimal; color: #444444;"&gt;[S39] Medieval, royalty, nobility family group sheets (filmed 1996), Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints. Family History Department
2 CONC . Medieval Family History Unit, (Manuscript. Salt Lake City, Utah : Filmed by the Genealogical Society of Utah, 1996), FHL film 1553977-1553985..&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li style="margin: 0px 0px 0px 30px; padding: 2px 0px; list-style-type: deci
