1 DATE December 7, 1709
1 PLAC Bucks County, Pennsylvania
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;From Wills: Abstracts, Book C&amp;nbsp;: 1705 - 1714: Philadelphia Co, PA:&lt;/p&gt;<
2 CONC /line><line>&lt;p&gt;"ALBERSON, WILLIAM. Bucks Co. December 7, 1709. January 17, 1710. Children Benjamin, Josiah, William, Abraham, Ann, Cassandra, and Rebecca Sotterthoit. Grandchildren names not given. Sons-in-law Jervis Stockdale and John Keighn
2 CONC . Friends George Goldsmith and Walter Forrest. Executrix: Wife Hannah. Witnesses: Thomas Millard, Christ. Vandergraft and John Kaighn."&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;Note: Hannah not the mother of William's four eldest children. Their mother possi
2 CONC bly was a woman named Jane who signed with him at several Haddonfield marriages.&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
