2 TITL Ware Family Migration to Five SW Counties of Ohio
1 _OID 75125f70-c240-49ad-a720-aa8dd500cb71
1 _DSCR All of the early Ware Families that migrated from New Jersey to Ohio, migrated to the Clermont and Warren counties. Mary Albertson Ware (Widow) migrated west to Warren county in 1819-1820 along with her single children and her married son Jesse (m
2 CONC d Mary Pease). From Warren county, these families moved to Preble county. Nancy Ann Ware Carter migrated to Bethel, Clermont county abt 1816 and died there in 1840. Isaiah M. Ware Sr. along with his sons Kimble, Isaiah M. Jr. and others migrated t
2 CONC o Clermont county and then later moved to Butler county, then to Cincinnati, Hamilton county. Andrew M. Ware (Isaiah Sr's brother) migrated to Ohio eventually settling in the Cincinnati area. The mass migration of these Ware families westward was n
2 CONC o easy task. It took their combined funds and mutual support to be successful.
