1 _OID dbc3fad2-f6e9-4155-92f1-eef5e9eb1d1d
1 DATE circa 1710
1 PLAC Nantucket, Massachusetts
1 _DSCR Quaker burials on Nantucket
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: large;"&gt;Friends First Burial Ground, began about 1705, 1rst paragraph, then Quaker Burial Ground, began in 1730, 2nd paragraph &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: #ffdead
2 CONC ; font-family: 'comic sans ms'; font-size: small;"&gt;By way of postscript, it may be stated that the first burial ground of the Quakers was situated just to the west of Elihu Coleman's house on the old Madeket road, but, left for many years withou
2 CONC t a stone, a fence, or any kind of protection, it has long been unrecognizable, and no one could imagine that it had ever been a place of interment.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&l
2 CONC t;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'comic sans ms'; font-size: small; background-color: #ffdead;"&gt;In the latest burying place of the Quakers, at the corner of Upper Main and Saratoga Streets, with the exception of a few small markers in the Hic
2 CONC ksite section, there is nothing to indicate that, beneath the weedy grass of the enclosure, between nine and ten thousand human bodies are buried without even a flower to mark any of their graves, and yet there is none of the older Nantucket famili
2 CONC es whose ancestors are not sleeping their last sleep in this neglected field.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'comic sans ms'; font-size: small; background-color: #ffdead;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&g
2 CONC t;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong style="font-family: 'comic sans ms'; font-size: medium; text-align: -webkit-center; background-color: #ffdead;"&gt;Quaker History&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Extracted From&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Nantucket; a History&lt;br&gt;
2 CONC Douglas-Lithgow, R.A.&lt;br&gt;New York. G.P. Putman's Sons, Knickerbocker Press&lt;br&gt;1914.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;&lt;em&gt;[Transcribed by Coralynn Brown]&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/stron
2 CONC g&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
